{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgH9eRVkvX9rLzZMiqjXm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Yes to both.** Tessmark Clinical Supply is flagged \"Conflict - cross-fund review\", so it is on hold until cross-fund clearance. The $55M check would also take Fund IV over its 35% concentration guideline in Specialty Distribution.\n\n| # | Check | Counterpart / area | Fund | Distance / exposure | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Portfolio conflict | Pinewick Dermatology Partners | Fund III (since 2020-07-01) | 1 commercial link | **CONFLICT - cross-fund review** |\n| 2 | Concentration | Specialty Distribution | Fund IV | $385M (32.1%) → **$440M (36.7%)** vs 35% guideline | **Breach, over by $20M** (headroom $35M) |\n| 3 | Portfolio conflict | Ironvale Testing Group | Fund IV (since 2024-03-15) | 2 commercial links | Shared counterparty (informational) |\n| 4 | Concentration | Testing, Inspection & Certification | Fund IV | $150M (12.5%), unchanged | Within guideline |\n| 5 | Concentration | Healthcare Services | Fund IV | $110M (9.2%), unchanged | Within guideline |\n| 6 | Concentration | Tech-Enabled Business Services | Fund IV | $0M (0.0%) | Within guideline |\n\n1. Tessmark Clinical Supply supplies Pinewick Dermatology Partners, which Fund III has held since 2020-07-01. That is 1 commercial link away.\n2. Fund IV holds Tullmere Chemical Distribution ($140M), Flintmoor Industrial Supply ($125M) and Primdale Ingredients Co ($120M), which is $385M or 32.1% of the fund. Adding the $55M Tessmark check makes it $440M or 36.7%, which is $20M over the 35% guideline.\n3. Tessmark Clinical Supply supplies Ravenholt Engineering Group, which buys from Ironvale Testing Group (Fund IV, since 2024-03-15). That is 2 links away, so it is for information only and does not block the deal.\n4. Fund IV holds Ironvale Testing Group ($150M), 12.5% of the fund, within the guideline.\n5. Fund IV holds Quillmont Physical Therapy ($110M), 9.2% of the fund, within the guideline.\n6. Fund IV has no current holding in this area.\n\nTo bid at $55M, the deal needs cross-fund clearance on the Pinewick link. It also needs either a check of $35M or less, or a waiver of the guideline.\n\nA CRM or SQL screen would miss both findings. The conflict runs through a supplier relationship with a Fund III company, not through anything Fund IV owns directly. The breach only shows up once the new check is added to the existing holdings in the same area."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1178,"cache_read_input_tokens":32905,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1178,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e1f7bc6-b78f-4251-8e11-cbfe96b991c0","uuid":"b786e281-a6ec-47ab-ac08-6f18711b5e52","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:52:56.355Z","request_id":"req_011CgH9eRCQdFWnLVxMrXBt4"}
